# Audio Konverter

A simple, modern audio converter for Windows, macOS and Linux, powered by ffmpeg.
Drop in files or whole folders, pick a format and a preset, done.

![Audio Konverter screenshot](docs/screenshot.png)

**[Download the latest version](https://github.com/Olcay91/Audio-Konverter/releases/latest)**

## Features

- **Formats:** MP3, AAC (M4A), Opus, Ogg Vorbis, FLAC, ALAC, WAV and AIFF. Reads practically every audio format.
- **Presets** for every format, plus your own (bitrate or quality, sample rate, bit depth, channels).
- **Never upsamples:** sample rate, bit depth and channels are only ever reduced.
- **Skips pointless conversions**, e.g. FLAC to FLAC with the same settings or MP3 to a higher MP3 bitrate, and tells you why.
- **Keeps your tags and cover art** (cover art for MP3, AAC, ALAC and FLAC).
- **Folders in, folders out:** recreates the folder structure or saves next to the originals, with a file name template (`{artist}/{album}/{track} {title}`).
- **Fast:** converts several files in parallel.
- **German and English** user interface, light and dark mode, accent colors.
- **Updates itself** with one click.
- ffmpeg is included, nothing else to install.

## Installation

| System | Download |
|---|---|
| Windows 10/11 | Installer (`…-setup.exe`) or portable ZIP |
| macOS 11+ (Apple silicon) | `…_aarch64.dmg` |
| macOS 10.15+ (Intel) | `…_x64.dmg` |
| Linux | `.AppImage` (portable) or `.deb` |

The app isn't signed with a paid certificate yet, so Windows SmartScreen and macOS Gatekeeper
will warn you on first launch. The [release notes](https://github.com/Olcay91/Audio-Konverter/releases/latest)
explain how to open it anyway.

## Building from source

You need Rust (stable), Node.js 20+ and ffmpeg in your `PATH`.

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # run with hot reload
npm run build    # build the app
```

Developer documentation (German): [docs/ENTWICKLUNG.md](docs/ENTWICKLUNG.md)

## Built with

[Tauri 2](https://tauri.app) (Rust) · [Svelte 5](https://svelte.dev) · [FFmpeg](https://ffmpeg.org)

The bundled ffmpeg is a lean, audio-only LGPL build. See [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

